

  JYT-UX-W03 Hall draft submission and recovery adapter
    ✔ accepts server-declared plain-text input capability without exposing it as an output format (105ms)
    ✔ persists a validated DRAFT-v1 create receipt with exact fixed inputs
    ✔ quotes If-Match, keeps local input on a 412, and asks the user to reload
    ✔ preserves the W02 discard action and sends its exact revision/key
    ✔ persists only a scope-isolated non-sensitive submit intent, locks the acknowledged draft, and blocks a second POST
    ✔ uses the original key only for unknown submit reconciliation and never crosses account scope
    ✔ keeps the unknown original key locked through a rejected reconciliation and reuses it after reauthorization
    ✔ hides the prior owner on logout while retaining the isolated unknown key for reauthorization
    ✔ refuses persistence and submission without a stable owner/client scope
    ✔ accepts the frozen TASK_ACTION receipt shape without mixing it into a private case
    ✔ releases deterministic submit failures for correction while retaining only uncertain failures
    ✔ reads only the frozen private-execution results path and preserves fixed output versions
    ✔ shows an empty result set only for a nonterminal execution and rejects malformed committed output
    ✔ uses the API cursor limit of 300 rather than an arbitrary ID limit

  JYT-UX-W05 frozen TASK_CREATE receipt boundaries
    ✔ accepts nullable optional DRAFT-v1 fields in saved drafts and recoverable summaries
    ✔ accepts TASK_CREATE without execution, keeps exact string taskVersion, and never submits twice
    ✔ locks invalid task receipts and never confuses private, TASK_ACTION and TASK_CREATE shapes
    ✔ retains POST503 intent through real identity cleanup and GET401/403, then reads the same task key
    ✔ rechecks the shared scope intent before another retained pane can post
    ✔ does not let a late reconciliation of an acknowledged task erase another pane's newer unknown intent
    ✔ allows explicit correction after original POST422 but not after a refused formal detail read

  JYT-UX-W05 field-level DRAFT-v1 limits
    ✔ rejects 201-character titles locally before create or CAS replacement and keeps the saved draft
    ✔ loads and saves legitimate 16001–20000-character instructions with exact CAS and Unicode code-point title limits
    ✔ serializes unselected agent and MIME as null, not invalid optional exact empty strings

  JYT-UX-W03 HallDraftEditor boundary
    ✔ receives the stable owner/client scope from the production Hall path rather than an epoch
    ✔ mounts the production component with its empty default draft and exposes the first save action (64ms)
    ✔ mounts fixed private results, hides unavailable actions, and creates a revision from the exact output reference (51ms)

  JYT-UX-W05 real editor source restoration
    ✔ restores the exact saved draft revision through GET without creating a replacement (149ms)
    ✔ restores formal draft editing without presenting a private-submission confirmation (192ms)
    ✔ opens PRIVATE_CASE progress without fabricating a submission receipt or resubmitting (81ms)
    ✔ keeps LEGACY_EXECUTION read-only and reads its real execution endpoint (93ms)
    ✔ does not turn an inaccessible draft into a fresh editable form (165ms)
    ✔ rejects a different draft ID returned for an exact overview reference (73ms)
    ✔ creates a formal draft without agent/format/material inputs and opens the exact real formal task after one POST (95ms)
    ✔ preserves oversized restored formal text and saves it without truncation, but requires correction before confirmation (82ms)
    ✔ keeps incompatible formal agent/format/fixed inputs until explicit removal and withdraws saved-snapshot authorization on edit (117ms)
    ✔ never erases immutable formal source/conversation metadata or creates a replacement draft to bypass it (162ms)
    ✔ retains full private CREATE editing, selected target and fixed inputs instead of imposing formal limits (97ms)
    ✔ renders only capability-backed human-readable formats, preserving unsupported old MIME without replacing it (92ms)
    ✔ submits an empty private format as server-supported text and shows the actual default on confirmation (112ms)
    ✔ uses the first service-supported format only when text is unavailable (111ms)
    ✔ keeps a restored supported non-text format instead of silently replacing it with the default (58ms)
    ✔ keeps long saved private text and format visible when capabilities are unavailable, without allowing submission (68ms)

  W04 saved-source exit boundary
    ✔ keeps fixed file source and edited text on failed save, then acknowledges only the saved snapshot (54ms)

  JYT-UX-W02 visible draft-step regressions
    ✔ requires an explicitly selected visible agent, exposes confirm save, and keeps authorization disabled after a failed save (62ms)
    ✔ keeps material selection count and actions in a bounded footer while the long list owns scrolling (77ms)
    ✔ allows cancelling a selected fixed v1 after workspace latest advances to v2, and never offers newer result versions (69ms)

  JYT-UX-W05 independent Hall read model
    ✔ uses a query-free overview and retains unknown counts and exact source refs
    ✔ retains partial/failed sources without hiding the other source or pretending empty
    ✔ continues only the requested source with its opaque cursor (not the ID length limit)
    ✔ retries a failed page with the same cursor while showing retained data as unconfirmed
    ✔ clears all summaries after 401 without issuing any mutation
    ✔ clears all summaries after 403 without issuing any mutation
    ✔ fences late account A results and never displays them for account B
    ✔ does not fetch without a stable scope and clears data on lifecycle identity cleanup
    ✔ rejects cross-partition source types and mismatched evidence without losing valid partitions
    ✔ loads a canonical formal task by ref instead of using an overview summary as a task
    ✔ reports a read error, not a successful empty overview, on 503 or invalid envelope
    ✔ preserves compatible private mark and formal review evidence without conflating action types
    ✔ loads archive by independent applicable source and retains an explicit draft archive error instead of empty success

